---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Doc from '../components/legal/Doc.astro';
const updated = '29 October 2026';
// Drafts stay out of search until counsel signs off and every placeholder is filled (design/legal/README.md).
const draft = true;
---

<Base title="Terms of use · Comarket" description="The rules for using comarket.si and joining the Comarket waitlist, and the general terms behind every Comarket agreement." stage="none" noindex={draft}>
  <Doc
    title="Terms of use"
    lede="The rules for using this site and the waitlist. Part B holds the general terms that also sit under the Brand and Creator agreements."
    updated={updated}
    draft={draft}
    current="/terms"
  >
    <div class="short">
      <b>The short version</b>
      <ul>
        <li>Joining the waitlist is free and doesn't commit you to anything. It holds your place; it isn't a contract for our services.</li>
        <li>The brands, creators, posts and numbers on this site are examples, not promises of results.</li>
        <li>Use the site fairly: no bots, scraping, fake sign-ups or attacks.</li>
        <li>When the platform opens, brands sign the <a href="/brand-terms">Brand Agreement</a> and creators the <a href="/creator-terms">Creator Agreement</a>. Part B of this page applies to both.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are and what these terms cover</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.1</span>These terms are an agreement between you and [[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]], a [[ENTITY TYPE AND JURISDICTION]]
      registered under number [[COMPANY NUMBER]], with its registered office at [[REGISTERED ADDRESS]] ("Comarket", "we",
      "us"). Our VAT number is [[VAT NUMBER]]. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:[[CONTACT EMAIL]]">[[CONTACT EMAIL]]</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.2</span>Part A covers comarket.si, its subdomains and the waitlist (together, the "Site"). Part B holds
      general terms that apply to Part A and to every other Comarket agreement, including the
      <a href="/brand-terms">Brand Agreement</a> and the <a href="/creator-terms">Creator Agreement</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.3</span>By using the Site or joining the waitlist, you accept these terms. If you act for a company, you
      accept them for that company and confirm that you are allowed to. Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>,
      <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> and <a href="/acceptable-use">acceptable use policy</a> also apply.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Part A: using the Site</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">2.1</span>You may browse the Site and use its features, such as the storefront preview, the handle
      check and the calculators, for your own evaluation of Comarket.
    </p>
    <p><span class="n">2.2</span>You must not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use bots, scripts or other automated means to sign up, check handles, request previews or collect content, except search engines that follow our robots rules;</li>
      <li>sign up with someone else's email, or claim a handle or a brand you have no right to represent;</li>
      <li>try to break, overload or get around the Site's security, rate limits or bot checks, or probe it for weaknesses without our written permission (report security issues to [[CONTACT EMAIL]]);</li>
      <li>use the preview to fetch sites in order to attack, scrape or burden them; or</li>
      <li>break the law or the <a href="/acceptable-use">acceptable use policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. The waitlist</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.1</span><b>Who can join.</b> You must be at least 18 and joining for a business or for your own work as a
      creator. Brands must be able to bind the brand they name.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.2</span><b>What joining means.</b> Joining holds your place. It is not an order for our services and does
      not oblige you or us to enter into any further agreement. We decide when and in what order to open places, and we may
      open them out of order, for example by category, country or fit, or to stop abuse. Your pass number has no cash value
      and can't be sold or transferred.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.3</span><b>Creator handles.</b> When you claim a handle (such as comarket.si/yourname), we keep it for you
      while you are on the waitlist and, once you open an account, under the Creator Agreement. A handle is a permission to use
      an address, not property. We may refuse or withdraw a handle that impersonates someone, uses a name or trademark you
      have no right to, is offensive or misleading, or is one we need for the Site, and we will offer you another. You can't
      sell or transfer a handle.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.4</span><b>Prices shown to brands.</b> We record the fee rates a brand was shown when it joined. If the
      rates in the Brand Agreement you later sign are higher, we will apply the rates you were shown for
      [[FOUNDING RATE PERIOD]].
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.5</span><b>Referral links.</b> You may share the referral link we give you. Don't spam it, buy sign-ups,
      or create entries for people who didn't ask. We record which pass a sign-up came from. Any reward for referrals will be
      announced with its own rules; none is promised by these terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.6</span><b>Emails.</b> We send a confirmation, and one email when your spot opens. We send other news
      only if you agree to receive it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.7</span><b>Leaving.</b> You can leave the waitlist at any time by emailing [[CONTACT EMAIL]]. We may remove
      an entry that breaks these terms or looks automated or fake.
    </p>

    <h2>4. What you give us</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">4.1</span>Give accurate information. You remain responsible for what you submit.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">4.2</span>You let us use what you submit (for example your website, brand name or handle) to hold your
      place, to build a preview of your storefront, and to contact you about Comarket. For a preview, our server reads your
      website's public homepage. A preview is a mock-up; it is not a live page and isn't published.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">4.3</span>If you send us ideas or feedback, we may use them without owing you anything. You don't have to
      send any.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Examples on the Site</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.1</span>The brands, creators, posts, storefronts, sales and earnings shown on the Site are fictional
      examples made to show how Comarket works. They are not testimonials, typical results or promises. What a brand sells
      and what a creator earns depend on the product, the offer, the audience and many other things we don't control.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.2</span>Fee rates and terms stated on the Site summarise the Brand and Creator agreements. If a summary
      and an agreement differ, the agreement applies.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Our rights in the Site</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">6.1</span>We, or our licensors, own the Site, its design, code, text, images, 3D models and the Comarket
      name and marks. These terms give you no rights in them beyond using the Site as allowed here. You may not copy the Site
      or its storefront designs for another service.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Other sites and services</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.1</span>The Site links to services we don't run, such as X for sharing your pass and, later, Stripe.
      Their own terms and privacy policies apply, and we are not responsible for them.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Availability and changes to the Site</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">8.1</span>The Site is pre-launch. We may change, pause or withdraw any part of it, including the waitlist,
      at any time. We don't promise it will always be available or free of errors.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Our liability for the Site</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">9.1</span>The Site and the waitlist are free and provided "as is". To the extent the law allows, we give no
      warranties about them, express or implied, including fitness for a purpose and non-infringement.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">9.2</span>To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for lost profits, revenue, business, data or
      goodwill, or for indirect or consequential loss, arising from the Site or the waitlist, and our total liability to you
      for them is limited to [[SITE LIABILITY CAP]].
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">9.3</span>Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for
      fraud, for gross negligence or wilful misconduct, or for anything else that can't be limited by law. If you are a
      consumer, you keep every right that the law of the country where you live gives you and that can't be waived.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Ending your use</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">10.1</span>You can stop using the Site at any time. We may suspend or end your access, or remove your
      waitlist entry, if you break these terms, if the law requires it, or if we stop running the waitlist. Sections 4.3, 5,
      6, 9 and Part B survive.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Part B: general terms</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">11.1</span><b>Where these apply.</b> Part B applies to Part A and to every Comarket agreement that refers to
      it, including the Brand Agreement and the Creator Agreement (each an "Agreement"). If Part B and an Agreement differ, the
      Agreement applies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">11.2</span><b>Reading these terms.</b> Headings and short versions are for convenience and don't change the
      meaning. "Including" means including without limitation. "Writing" includes email. A reference to a law includes it as
      amended or replaced.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">12.1</span>Keep your login details safe and your account information accurate. You are responsible for
      what happens under your account, unless it happens because we failed to keep our systems secure. Tell us at once at
      [[CONTACT EMAIL]] if you think someone else has used your account.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">12.2</span>An account is for the person or business that opened it. Don't share it, sell it or open
      several to get around a limit or a decision we have made.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes to these terms and to an Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">13.1</span>We may change Part B or an Agreement. For a change that affects brands or creators, we will give
      at least 15 days' notice by email and in the product, longer where the change needs technical or commercial
      adjustments from you, and we will say what is changing.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">13.2</span>If you don't accept a change, you may end the Agreement before the change takes effect, without
      any charge for ending it. Fees and earnings for sales made before the end stay payable under the Agreement.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">13.3</span>We may make a change sooner where the law or a regulator requires it, or to deal with an
      unforeseen and imminent risk of fraud, malware, spam, a data breach or another security threat. We will tell you as
      soon as we can.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">13.4</span>Changes to Part A apply from the date posted on this page, and only to use of the Site after
      that date.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Confidentiality</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">14.1</span>Each party will keep the other's non-public business information confidential, use it only for
      the Agreement, and share it only with people who need it for that purpose and are bound to keep it confidential. This
      doesn't apply to information that is or becomes public through no fault of the receiving party, that it already had or
      developed independently, or that it must disclose by law (after giving notice where allowed). The duty lasts for the
      Agreement and three years after it ends, and for trade secrets as long as they remain secret.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Notices</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">15.1</span>We send notices to the email address on your account or waitlist entry, or in the product.
      You send notices to <a href="mailto:[[CONTACT EMAIL]]">[[CONTACT EMAIL]]</a>. A formal legal notice to us must also be
      sent by post or courier to [[REGISTERED ADDRESS]]. An email notice is received when sent, unless the sender gets an
      error message.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Complaints and mediation</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">16.1</span>If you have a complaint about Comarket, including about a decision to restrict, suspend or end
      your account, a decision about a sale, or how we match brands and creators, write to [[CONTACT EMAIL]] with the details.
      We will acknowledge it within 5 business days, consider it properly and tell you the outcome and our reasons, normally
      within 30 days. Using this process is free and doesn't stop you going to court.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">16.2</span>If a dispute with a brand or creator acting as a business isn't resolved through complaints,
      we are willing to try mediation in good faith with [[MEDIATORS]]. We will pay a reasonable share of the mediator's costs.
      Mediation is voluntary and doesn't affect either side's right to go to court.
    </p>

    <h2>17. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">17.1</span>Before starting proceedings, each party will raise the dispute in writing and both will try for
      30 days to settle it by talking, except where urgent relief is needed to protect rights or confidential information.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">17.2</span>These terms, each Agreement and any dispute about them, including non-contractual disputes, are
      governed by the law of [[GOVERNING LAW]], without regard to its conflict-of-law rules. The United Nations Convention on
      Contracts for the International Sale of Goods does not apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">17.3</span>The courts of [[COURTS]] have exclusive jurisdiction, except that either party may seek urgent
      relief, or bring a claim for unpaid amounts, in any court that has jurisdiction.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">17.4</span>If you are a consumer, you may bring proceedings in the courts where you live, and the choice of
      law in 17.2 doesn't take away the protection of mandatory consumer law of the country where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>18. Everything else</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.1</span><b>Events outside our control.</b> Neither party is liable for delay or failure caused by events
      beyond its reasonable control, such as outages of internet, hosting or payment providers, or acts of government. This
      doesn't excuse paying money owed.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.2</span><b>Transfer.</b> You may not transfer an Agreement without our written consent. We may transfer
      an Agreement to a company in our group or to a buyer of our business, and will tell you. We may use subcontractors and
      remain responsible for them.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.3</span><b>Relationship.</b> The parties are independent. Nothing creates a partnership, joint venture,
      employment or agency, except the limited payment collection role described in the Brand and Creator agreements.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.4</span><b>Whole agreement.</b> Each Agreement, with the documents it refers to, is the whole agreement on
      its subject. Neither party relies on any statement not in it, but this doesn't limit liability for fraud.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.5</span><b>Severability and waiver.</b> If a court finds part of these terms unenforceable, the rest
      still applies, and that part applies to the extent it can. Not enforcing a right now doesn't waive it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.6</span><b>Third parties.</b> Only the parties to an Agreement can enforce it, unless it says otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.7</span><b>Sanctions and export.</b> You confirm that you are not a sanctioned person or acting for one,
      and that you won't use Comarket in breach of sanctions or export laws.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">18.8</span><b>Language.</b> These terms are written in English. If we provide a translation and it differs,
      the English version applies, unless the law requires otherwise.
    </p>
  </Doc>
  <Footer />
</Base>
